<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- MapControlsStripSeparator — the mark between tool GROUPS on the tools tier (MapControlsStrip): a small
     GRID OF DOTS, centred in its slot. Every part of its shape is a DP so it can be re-tuned at the use site
     (or here, for all of them) without touching the strip.

       (◗)(✈)(⚗)   ⁘   (⌕)   ⁘   (⌸)(◎)   · · · · · · · · · · ·   [KTLX Oklahoma City ˅]
                   ↑                        · · · · · · · · · · ·
                   Columns × Rows (3 × 3)   · · · · · · · · · · ·   ← FillWidth: Rows kept, as many columns as
                                                                      the host-set Width holds, centred
                   · · ·     DotSize 1.5 · DotGap 2.5  →  a 9.5 × 9.5 block at 3 × 3
                   · · ·     MARGINS are the host's, and GENEROUS on purpose: the gap is what groups the tools
                   · · ·

     DPs: Columns (3) · Rows (3) · FillWidth · DotSize (1.5) · DotGap (2.5) · Brush.
     ⚠️ The grid is REBUILT only when the dot COUNT changes; a FillWidth separator re-lays out on every width
     change its host makes, and most of those don't change the count.
     ⚠️ DELIBERATELY FAINT (~16% of the text colour — MapControlsStripSeparatorDotBrush below): it must read as
     structure, never as one more tool. The two stock steps were both wrong — Tertiary sat too close to the
     glyphs, Disabled (36%) still did. Picked from a mockup (2026-09-29), 2 px lines → dots.
     ⚠️ Brush null = that THEME brush, applied through DotStyle — never resolved in C# (it would snapshot the OS
     theme, not the app's). A set Brush is a LOCAL Fill on each dot; clearing it hands the style back.
     ⚠️ It is NOT a line across the tier: the tier has no seams (see MapControlsStrip's header). -->
<UserControl x:Class="Anvil.Controls.Primitives.MapControlsStripSeparator"
             xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008"
             xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
             mc:Ignorable="d"
             IsTabStop="False"
             IsHitTestVisible="False"
             VerticalAlignment="Center">
    <UserControl.Resources>
        <ResourceDictionary>
            <ResourceDictionary.ThemeDictionaries>
                <ResourceDictionary x:Key="Default">
                    <SolidColorBrush x:Key="MapControlsStripSeparatorDotBrush" Color="#29FFFFFF"/> <!-- ~16% white -->
                </ResourceDictionary>
                <ResourceDictionary x:Key="Light">
                    <SolidColorBrush x:Key="MapControlsStripSeparatorDotBrush" Color="#29000000"/> <!-- ~16% black -->
                </ResourceDictionary>
            </ResourceDictionary.ThemeDictionaries>
            <Style x:Key="DotStyle" TargetType="Ellipse">
                <Setter Property="Fill" Value="{ThemeResource MapControlsStripSeparatorDotBrush}"/>
            </Style>
        </ResourceDictionary>
    </UserControl.Resources>

    <!-- The dots are built in code (BuildDots): Columns × Rows, or FillWidth's count. Centred in the slot. -->
    <Grid x:Name="Dots" HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
</UserControl>
